From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: office <office@localhost>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH] proof: Uzbek and Russian text tagged English is not flagged as English misspellings

Documents made by generators tag every run en-US, so every Uzbek word got a red squiggle. As Word's "detect language
automatically" does, a paragraph under the English tag is judged by its text (the Vietnamese rule of vi.rs, extended): mostly
Cyrillic is Russian (own dictionary) or, with an Uzbek-only letter (Сћ Т› Т“ Ті), Uzbek (no tools: no marks); Latin text whose words
carry o'/g' or are frequent Uzbek words (va, bilan, uchun, hujjat...) is Uzbek; and a paragraph with at least one such word of
which three quarters of four or more words are unknown to the English dictionary is Uzbek too. New proof::uz; check_text_with
applies the result to the English spans and the default (English typos elsewhere are still flagged).
---

